1. Set Up Your Environment
Install a local server like XAMPP or WAMP.
Create a MySQL database and table to store the form data.
2. Create the HTML Form
Copy code
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AJAX Form Submission</title>
    <script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.6.0.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    <form id="myForm">
        <label for="name">Name:</label>
        <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required>
        <br>
        <label for="email">Email:</label>
        <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required>
        <br>
        <button type="submit">Submit</button>
    </form>
    <div id="response"></div>

    <script>
        $(document).ready(function () {
            $('#myForm').on('submit', function (e) {
                e.preventDefault(); // Prevent form from refreshing the page
                $.ajax({
                    url: 'submit.php',
                    type: 'POST',
                    data: $(this).serialize(),
                    success: function (response) {
                        $('#response').html(response); // Display server response
                    },
                    error: function () {
                        $('#response').html('An error occurred.');
                    }
                });
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>

3. Create the PHP Script (submit.php)
<?php
if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST') {
    $name = $_POST['name'];
    $email = $_POST['email'];

    // Database connection
    $conn = new mysqli('localhost', 'root', '', 'your_database_name');

    if ($conn->connect_error) {
        die('Connection failed: ' . $conn->connect_error);
    }

    // Insert data into the database
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("INSERT INTO your_table_name (name, email) VALUES (?, ?)");
    $stmt->bind_param("ss", $name, $email);

    if ($stmt->execute()) {
        echo "Data submitted successfully!";
    } else {
        echo "Error: " . $stmt->error;
    }

    $stmt->close();
    $conn->close();
}
?>

4. Create the MySQL Table

Run the following SQL query in your MySQL database:
CREATE DATABASE your_database_name;

USE your_database_name;

CREATE TABLE your_table_name (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
);

5. Test the Form
Start your local server.
Place the files in the server's root directory (e.g., htdocs for XAMPP).
Open the form in your browser and submit it. The data should be saved in your MySQL database.

